@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+## Why
+
+Customers ask to cancel bookings, and the desk has no way to do it. The refund rule is already agreed in `rental-cancellation-policy`; the operation that applies it does not exist yet.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `cancel(bookingId, at)` to the rental service. It cancels the booking at time `at` and returns `{ bookingId, refund }`.
+- The refund follows the existing policy: zero when `at` is less than 24 hours before the booking's start, otherwise the full booking total.
+- A cancelled booking stops holding its equipment, so `book` and `availability` treat the item as free for that period again.
+- A booking can be cancelled only once; unknown booking ids, repeat cancellations and invalid `at` throw and change nothing.
+- Update the README, which says cancellation is not implemented.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `rental-booking`: adds the cancellation operation and releases the equipment of a cancelled booking.
+- `rental-cancellation-policy`: the policy now applies to the cancellation operation (drops the "not yet offered" note).
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/rental.ts` (service interface and implementation), `src/rental.test.ts` (replaces the test asserting no `cancel` is exposed), `README.md`.
+- No new dependencies.
